racle": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-gate-clarity.md", ".prawduct/changes/gate-clarity.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "No recorded suite run on the integrated head: test-status is stale after the develop merge", "recommendation": "`prawduct-hook test-status` exits 1: `stale: evidence predates session (2026-11-12T04:34:30Z < 2026-11-12T16:13:17Z)`. The worktree's `.test-evidence.json` has `evidence_tree` 48a34168, which matches neither 87a91dbd's tree (5e0f6d09) nor the pre-merge gate-clarity head 6e83ac19 (7eeebd08). It is a pre-split floor record that still lists non-Python files under `changes_unjudged`/`changes_unchecked`. Merge 7c808658 came after that run and brought develop's changes to the two files this branch rewrites most, `plugin/lib/gates.py` (+179) and `plugin/bin/prawduct-hook` (+46), plus critic_consolidate, standing_block and telemetry. The merge had no conflicts, but nothing records that the combined code passes. Chunk 05's Done-when asks for exactly that: 'Suite green on the integrated head, recorded'. Fix (instance): run the suite on 87a91dbd (or its successor) and run `prawduct-hook test-evidence record` before the PR merges.", "files": ["plugin/lib/gates.py", "plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "warning", "title": "The Stop gate's 'excused imported files' NOTE goes to raw stderr, which reaches nobody at the exit-0 Stop where it fires", "recommendation": "`cmd_stop` prints the #1098 NOTE with `print(..., file=sys.stderr)`, and only when `not critic_would_block`, which is almost always an exit-0 Stop. The hook's own single owner for this channel says why that fails. `_deliver_stop_advisories`'s docstring reads: 'plain stdout/stderr at exit 0 is logged and reaches nobody'. User-visible text there goes through `host.emit_stop_advisory` (systemMessage), and at a blocking Stop it goes into the block reason through `_stop_advisories_in_block`. So on a pass, the excused files are reported to no one. That contradicts the code comment ('a pass that excused something is never silent about what it excused, or about who still owes it'), Chunk 03's deliverable ('The Stop blocker's render says so in one line'), and the change record's consumer note ('names the ones it excused'). `test_the_stop_hook_says_what_it_excused_in_one_line` asserts only `capsys` stderr at rc == 0, which is the channel that reaches nobody, so the test stays green either way. Scope: class. The cause is a Stop-hook advisory printed directly instead of through `_deliver_stop_advisories`, and the same shape exists outside this diff: the learnings-budget `NOTE: ... unchecked` lines (prawduct-hook ~3484, whose comment also says 'never silent'), the core-raise NOTE (~3491), and the Gate 2.5 mode NOTE (~4068). The fix needs one owner, not one more list entry. Append this NOTE to `stop_advisories` (a plain str reaches the user at exit 0 and rides the block reason at exit 2; choose `_LogOnlyAdvisory` only if it really is meant to be log-only). Point the test at the delivered channel (the emitted systemMessage). Pin the class with a test that `cmd_stop` writes no user-facing `NOTE:` outside `_deliver_stop_advisories`.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "tests/test_session_critic_gate.py"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "warning", "title": "_cached_diff_fn's docstring still says it is reached only by _attribute_free_steps, but this diff added two callers", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. Why it broke: the diff gave `gates._cached_diff_fn` new callers and left the docstring's reach claim as it was. The docstring (plugin/lib/gates.py, `_cached_diff_fn`) still says every production call site pairs it with `_tree_key_fn`, so it 'is reached only by `_attribute_free_steps`' at O(path length) calls. That is no longer true. `coverage_algebra.excused_gap_verdict` (the Stop gate's third arm) now sends up to EXCUSED_GAP_MAX_PAIRS whole-tree gap diffs per phase through it, and its own docstring relies on that memo ('the second phase's mostly answered by the caller's diff memo'). `coverage.explain_uncovered` also diffs through it, reaching it via `session_uncovered_cause` and via the PR gate's new `answer['_diff_fn']`. The learnings rule this rests on: 'A docstring or comment is a claim: before one states reach or a guarantee ('the one reader', 'never raises'), grep the callers'. The wrong action it invites: a maintainer who believes the memo only serves attribution trims or drops it, and every uncovered Stop then pays the third arm's diffs twice, against the P0 review-wall-clock norm. Fix: delete the 'reached only by' sentence, or make it relational (the memo serves every caller that diffs a pair within one gate call). Do not add a list of today's callers.", "files": ["plugin/lib/gates.py"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "warning", "title": "_reach rebuilds _find_path's evidence graph, and the third arm's relax-only soundness depends on the two copies staying identical", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. Why it broke: `excused_gap_verdict` needed a closure where `_find_path` gives a single path, so its new `_reach` re-derives the node set, review adjacency and free-edge relation instead of sharing them. The node set is `{start, other_end}` plus the edge endpoints, the free edges come from `_free_classes` or pairwise `_free_edge_files`, and the docstring itself says it is 'the same node set and the same free-edge relation `_find_path` searches'. That sameness is what `excused_gap_verdict` rests on: 'Every review edge and free edge used is one `coverage_verdict` would use'. No test compares the two relations. `test_the_key_form_agrees_with_the_pairwise_form` checks `_reach`'s key form against its own pairwise form, not against `_find_path`. The consequence: a future change to `_find_path`'s graph (which trees count as nodes, when an interval is free) that misses `_reach` lets this relax-only arm compose across edges `coverage_verdict` no longer grants. That fails open, in the gate that ends a session. Fix: extract one builder (e.g. `_evidence_graph(edges, endpoints, key_fn, diff_fn)` returning nodes, directed adjacency and free adjacency) that both `_find_path` and `_reach` consume. Alternatively, pin the property with a test: every non-gap step of an excused path is an edge `_find_path` would traverse on the same facts.", "files": ["plugin/lib/coverage_algebra.py"], "fid": "R-4"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 4, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "Governing-Artifact Reconciliation: every recorded disposition holds against the diff; the one partial gap is how the `changes_unchecked` deprecation is announced", "recommendation": "I checked each governed_by disposition against the code. Nothing writes outside the plugin's own state. 01 persists no memo. 02's explanation is wrapped twice and degrades to `CAUSE: unavailable (...)`. 03 narrows only after `_session_authored_paths` completes, declines on `None` and on an unlistable untracked set, relaxes only `uncovered` with `base_source == 'marker'`, and its pair cap can only deny. The PR gate's verdict path is unchanged, and no exit-code meaning changes. The #682 narrowing is the owner-ruled exception (2026-11-11, item 3; prior disposition R-4, not re-raised). One partial gap: api-contract's additive-first clause says a deprecation 'is signalled (stderr notice, kept working, removal deferred to a major), never silent'. `changes_unchecked` keeps working, but its deprecation shows up only in code comments and the change record's consumer note. `test-reference-verify` prints no stderr notice, and `plugin/docs/project-state-keys.md`, which documents the record's keys, does not mention the alias. The consumer note is a release-time signal, so this is not a silent removal. A one-line mention of the alias and its removal horizon in project-state-keys.md would close it.", "files": ["plugin/bin/test-reference-verify", "plugin/docs/project-state-keys.md"], "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "On a pre-split evidence record, verify-coverage labels non-Python files 'symbol-less or gone'", "recommendation": "A floor record written before #682 lists non-Python files in `changes_unjudged`. `verify_coverage` now reports that bucket as 'the verifier could not judge (changes_unjudged / deleted: symbol-less or gone)', which mislabels a `.swift` file, and `TestUnjudgedFilesAreNotGated` pins that text. Nothing gates on it, old records are replaced at the next `test-evidence record`, and no reader acts on the wording. Stating it so nobody spends an edit on it; no change wanted.", "files": ["plugin/lib/gates.py"], "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "explain_uncovered's `target` and format_uncovered_cause's `gate` encode one axis twice and can disagree", "recommendation": "`target='working'` must go with `gate='stop'`, and `target='head'` with `gate='pr'`. Both callers pair them correctly today. A third caller that mismatches them gets a suite-coupled list rendered as '(in this gate's span)', or the reverse. Simpler: have `explain_uncovered` record its target in the returned dict and let `format_uncovered_cause` read it from there. No change is required now.", "files": ["plugin/lib/coverage.py", "plugin/lib/gates.py"], "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "The diff adds coverage._shown for path elision, then writes two more inline copies beside it", "recommendation": "The 'first three, then (+N more)' rendering has three copies in this diff: `coverage._shown` / `_CAUSE_PATHS_SHOWN`, `gates._imported_history_verdict`'s `own` list, and `cmd_stop`'s `imported` NOTE in prawduct-hook. The pattern also recurs across plugin/lib from before this branch. Each copy is one line, and only the cap can drift, so this is cosmetic. Reusing `coverage._shown` at the two new sites would make the cap a single value.", "files": ["plugin/lib/gates.py", "plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/lib/coverage.py"], "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "transfer_remedy takes three parallel lists unpacked from one explain_uncovered dict", "recommendation": "`transfer_remedy(transfer, reason, uncommitted, *, untracked, index_deleted)` receives `explained['uncommitted']`, `explained['untracked']` and `explained['index_deleted']` from its only caller that passes them. Passing the explanation, or a small 'working-tree state' value, would keep the subset invariant (untracked and index_deleted are subsets of uncommitted) in one place. Optional.", "files": ["plugin/lib/gates.py"], "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "_uncommitted_paths makes three git calls for what one status read answers", "recommendation": "Three subprocesses get tracked edits, untracked files and index deletions: `git diff --no-renames HEAD`, `ls-files --others` and `diff --cached --diff-filter=D`. A single `git status --porcelain=v1 -z --no-renames --untracked-files=all` read would answer all three, and `gitstate.parse_porcelain_line` already exists. It runs only when an uncovered verdict renders, so the cost is small. It does sit oddly beside this plan's #937 theme of fewer subprocesses. No change is needed unless the render path proves hot.", "files": ["plugin/lib/coverage.py"], "oid": "O-6"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": "rule-unenforced: review/finding ids still ship in comments ('Critic R-5', 'rev-20261112T014213Z'), with no check owning the rule", "recommendation": "Rule (review-protocol.md 'Prose remedies', also recorded in the methodology's comment policy): 'Review and finding ids, chunk numbers and review history never belong in a shipped comment'. This diff adds `(Critic R-5)` in tests/test_coverage_algebra.py, `(Critic R-1, rev-20261112T014213Z)` and `(Critic R-5)` in tests/test_session_critic_gate.py, and `Renegotiated (Critic R-3, rev-20261112T014213Z)` in tests/test_verify_coverage_gate.py. The pattern predates this branch in other test files. Neither record_lint's CHECKS nor any test enforces the rule. To mechanise it, add a lint over added lines in plugin/ and tests/ that flags `Critic R-\\d+` and `rev-\\d{8}T` inside comments and docstrings. Rated as an observation because an instance is inert comment wording that nothing reads.", "files": ["tests/test_coverage_algebra.py", "tests/test_session_critic_gate.py", "tests/test_verify_coverage_gate.py"], "oid": "O-7"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "The batched diff-tree fallback is silent at runtime", "recommendation": "evidence.tree_diffs falls back to one git call per pair, discarding stderr, when the batch's rc is non-zero or _parse_diff_tree_stdin returns None. The verdict stays correct. Only the #937 cost saving disappears, and nothing at runtime shows it. The real-git call-count tests in tests/test_base_advance_diagnosis_cost.py would catch a regression in CI, and this lib has no debug-logging convention to follow, so no change is needed. If a slow Stop ever has to be diagnosed on a consumer's git version, a one-line debug channel here would show whether the batch ran.", "files": ["plugin/lib/evidence.py"], "oid": "O-8"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "verify-coverage's unjudged note mislabels a legacy record's non-Python files", "recommendation": "A record the floor wrote before the split lists non-Python files in changes_unjudged. verify_coverage counts them under the new label '(changes_unjudged / deleted: symbol-less or gone)', which is false for a .md or .ts file. Gating is unaffected and the record refreshes on the next test-evidence record, so nobody acts wrongly on it. The only consequence is a confusing line during the transition.", "files": ["plugin/lib/gates.py"], "oid": "O-9"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "Undated measurements in shipped docstrings and comments", "recommendation": "'~140 diffs, ~2.9 s of a warm Stop' appears in evidence.tree_diffs' docstring and a coverage.py comment with no date and no command that re-derives it. Nothing reads the number. The true dated figures are in the change record (2026-11-11). No edit is wanted.", "files": ["plugin/lib/evidence.py", "plugin/lib/coverage.py"], "oid": "O-10"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "No record that the changed Stop detection was run against this repo", "recommendation": "The plan's Verification Strategy and Chunk 05 promise a self-run of the changed Stop detection on this repo, following gates.md's rule 'Editing a runtime that governs the current session ... run the changed detection against this repo first'. The third arm is relax-only and can turn an uncovered verdict covered, which is exactly the case that rule protects against. No commit body, plan bullet or change-record line records that the run happened or what it returned. Nothing claims it was done, so no record is false. The plan's Integration bullet is the natural place for one line naming the command and the verdict it gave.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-gate-clarity.md"], "oid": "O-11"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "Records Pass: covered set and result", "recommendation": "Rated all three files_oracle records against the three bars: .prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-gate-clarity.md, .prawduct/changes/gate-clarity.md and .prawduct/owner-rulings.md. Checked the change record's shipped claims against the diff: batch fallback cases, the CAUSE causes and the unavailable render, the stash route with --include-untracked and the whole-tree route for index deletions, both names of a staged rename, the third arm's four narrowings and its 'imported-history excuse not applied:' suffix, the four-bucket partition, and the deprecated changes_unchecked alias. All hold. One exception is unstated: the arm stays silent when HEAD's tree never moved. No sync happened in that case, so no reader acts wrongly. The plan still marks the #1098 and #682 decisions 'Inferred, not ruled'. That is prior disposition R-4, accepted because owner-rulings.md records both rulings, and the plan has not changed since, so it is not re-raised. Nothing cleared a bar.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-gate-clarity.md", ".prawduct/changes/gate-clarity.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md"], "oid": "O-12"}], "duration_seconds": 900, "scope": "gate-clarity", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": "c599b926c4b824e27ef191ab5abd46a06fa7ebd9", "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-gate-clarity.md", ".prawduct/changes/gate-clarity.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md", "plugin/docs/project-state-keys.md", "plugin/skills/doctor/SKILL.md"], "chunk_graded": null, "chunks_graded": [], "plan_graded": null, "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": null, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "span": "full", "bounded_from": null, "span_reason": "base-moved", "dispatched_at": "2026-11-12T16:43:21Z"}}

